d release on the 2.x line.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `c8b8ab7878`: passed.\n\n## Notes\n- This is a minor-version bump within 2.x, so no major-version migration is involved. Reviewers may want to skim the fastjson 2.9.x changelog for any behavior changes that affect payment parsing.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4-pr", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created, but the response shows no reviewers, so alex wasn't added. I'll request alex's review explicitly.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KA9n6u4FbhFgb3NwrMfDRs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Fix:** CVE-2026-31337 is a high-severity unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. It affects versions below 2.9.4 and 3.0.0 through 3.0.x. I picked 2.9.4 because it's the fix on the 2.x line and avoids a major-version jump.\n- **Branch:** `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4`, with a one-line change to `requirements.txt`.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` on commit `c8b8ab7878` passed.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). The initial open call returned no reviewers, so I sent a separate review request to alex, which went through.\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}